---

## ⚙️ Key Design Decisions

### ArcGIS via CDN (not npm)
ArcGIS 4.x uses its own AMD module loader which conflicts with Vite's ESM bundler. The original app loaded it via `<script>` — we preserve this exactly. The `declare global { const require }` type declaration makes TypeScript accept this without any `any` suppression.

### CSS Custom Properties Preserved
Rather than converting ALL `var(--xxx)` tokens to Tailwind config values, we keep the CSS custom property system intact in [index.css](file:///d:/All%20projects/PM%20Surya%20Ghar%20Yojana/1.%20prototypes/solar_app_v4/react_frontend/src/index.css). This ensures the dark mode toggle works identically — adding/removing `dark-mode` from `<body>` updates all properties at once, exactly as the original.

### Tailwind v4 `@import "tailwindcss"`
Tailwind v4 uses the new `@import` syntax instead of `@tailwind base/components/utilities` directives.

### Flask Proxy
The [vite.config.ts](file:///d:/All%20projects/PM%20Surya%20Ghar%20Yojana/1.%20prototypes/solar_app_v4/react_frontend/vite.config.ts) proxy ensures `/api/*`, `/samples`, and `/sample/*` requests go to the Flask backend at `localhost:5000` during development — no CORS headers needed.

